>> title: Rib Tips
>> category: Smoked & Grilled
>> tags: pork, ribs, barbecue, smoker, low and slow
>> counters: Smokehouse
>> aka: tips, pork rib tips, bbq tips, barbeque rib tips, brisket-tip ends
>> servings: 4
>> time: 5 hr
>> pairs-with: barbecue-dip
>> step.2: rub
>> step.3: smoke 250°F (120°C) 3 hr
>> step.4: cut in 2-in pieces, toss
>> step.5: back in until the glaze tightens, 45 min

Bring the #smoker{} to 250°F (120°C) over hickory and hold it there.

Rub @pork rib tips{3%lb}(1.35 kg; the cartilage strip trimmed off spare ribs) with @yellow mustard{1%Tbs}, @kosher salt{2%tsp}, @dark brown sugar{2%Tbs}, @smoked paprika{1%Tbs}, @coarse black pepper{2%tsp}, and @cayenne{1/2%tsp}.

Smoke @&(~1)rubbed tips{} for ~smoke{3%hr}, until the cartilage has gone soft enough to bite through.

Cut @&(~1)smoked tips{} into 2-in pieces and toss them in a #pan{} with @barbecue sauce{1/2%cup}(120 mL) and @unsalted butter{2%Tbs}(28 g).

Return @&(~1)sauced tips{} to the smoker until the glaze tightens and catches at the edges, ~smoke{45%min}, and salt them with @flaky salt{1/2%tsp}.
